body:
### Version

5.1

### Context

The `io.vertx.core.spi.metrics.HttpClientMetrics#connected` method is invoked with the resolved address instead of the address provided by the user.

### Steps to reproduce

```patch
Index: vertx-core/src/test/java/io/vertx/tests/metrics/MetricsContextTest.java
IDEA additional info:
Subsystem: com.intellij.openapi.diff.impl.patch.CharsetEP
<+>UTF-8
===================================================================
diff --git a/vertx-core/src/test/java/io/vertx/tests/metrics/MetricsContextTest.java b/vertx-core/src/test/java/io/vertx/tests/metrics/MetricsContextTest.java
--- a/vertx-core/src/test/java/io/vertx/tests/metrics/MetricsContextTest.java	(revision 6e8dce0d988cc10f8cf6cefcdce6912329e72cc8)
+++ b/vertx-core/src/test/java/io/vertx/tests/metrics/MetricsContextTest.java	(date 1767885125309)
@@ -418,7 +418,7 @@
     AtomicReference<Context> expectedContext = new AtomicReference<>();
     AtomicReference<String> requestBeginCalled = new AtomicReference();
     AtomicBoolean responseEndCalled = new AtomicBoolean();
-    AtomicBoolean socketConnectedCalled = new AtomicBoolean();
+    AtomicReference<SocketAddress> socketConnectedCalled = new AtomicReference<>();
     AtomicBoolean socketDisconnectedCalled = new AtomicBoolean();
     AtomicBoolean bytesReadCalled = new AtomicBoolean();
     AtomicBoolean bytesWrittenCalled = new AtomicBoolean();
@@ -447,7 +447,7 @@
           }
           @Override
           public Void connected(SocketAddress remoteAddress, String remoteName) {
-            socketConnectedCalled.set(true);
+            socketConnectedCalled.set(remoteAddress);
             return null;
           }
           @Override
@@ -496,7 +496,7 @@
             close.onComplete(v2 -> {
               assertEquals("/the-uri", requestBeginCalled.get());
               assertTrue(responseEndCalled.get());
-              assertTrue(socketConnectedCalled.get());
+              assertEquals(SocketAddress.inetSocketAddress(8080, "localhost"), socketConnectedCalled.get());
               assertTrue(socketDisconnectedCalled.get());
               assertTrue(bytesReadCalled.get());
               assertTrue(bytesWrittenCalled.get());

```

Then run `io.vertx.tests.metrics.MetricsContextTest#testHttpClientRequestEventLoop` and you will see:

```
Starting test: MetricsContextTest#testHttpClientRequestEventLoop 
java.lang.AssertionError: expected:<localhost:8080> but was:<127.0.0.1:8080>
```

### Do you have a reproducer?

_No response_
